# Extrapolate the Impossible wants two cards with different names from outside the game, and Bot1 owns only two Lightning
# Bolts there: one name twice over is no pair, so there is no reveal to make and nothing is asked - Bot1 is not asked to
# choose, and neither is Bot2 (CR 608.2d). The positive control is
# extrapolate-the-impossible-reveals-two-and-puts-the-opponents-pick-into-hand, where a second name makes the question.

[Bot1 Deck]
Extrapolate the Impossible
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp
Island
Island
Island
Island x13

[Bot1 Sideboard]
Lightning Bolt
Lightning Bolt

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Extrapolate the Impossible.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp#2.Activate
Bot1.Pass
! Bot1.Choose
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Hand = Swamp; Island; Island; Island; Island
Bot1.Sideboard = Lightning Bolt; Lightning Bolt
Bot1.Graveyard = Extrapolate the Impossible
Stack.Count = 0
